{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>So he gathered them into custody for three days.</b> He did so in order to frighten them, and so that they would believe in him — that he fears Elohim, and out of that fear he releases them so that the people of their household will not die of famine. This is the meaning of \"But you, go, bring sustenance for the famine in your households\" (Genesis 42:19). And furthermore, that they would not agree to leave one behind, but only to save all of them."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:43:55.921919858Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}